W44-197 CfL Pass-2 Candidates B + C
====================================

git_commit: (will be filled in commit message)
host: AMD Ryzen 9 7950X (Linux 6.6.114.1-microsoft-standard-WSL2 / WSL2)
date: 2026-05-22 (UTC)
release_build: yes (best-of-5 wall ms)
features: __expert parallel butteraugli-loop ssim2-loop

Setup
-----

W44-197 ships two CfL improvements identified in the W44-189 deep audit:

- **Candidate B (Pass-2 LS-only at e=5/6 under Libjxl strategy)**:
  closes W44-189 D12 finding. Adds gate `cfl_pass2_ls_at_low_effort: bool`
  on `EncoderImprovementsCustom` + `ResolvedImprovements` + `EffortProfile`.
  `EncoderStrategy::Libjxl` sets it to `true`; all other strategies stay at
  `false` to preserve W44-29..W44-172 cost-model calibration.

  Wired at the Pass-2 dispatch site (`vardct/encoder.rs:~4920`):
    ```
    let effort_in_5_6 = self.effort == 5 || self.effort == 6;
    let pass2_fires = self.profile.cfl_two_pass
        || (self.profile.cfl_pass2_ls_at_low_effort && effort_in_5_6);
    let pass2_use_newton = self.profile.cfl_two_pass && self.profile.cfl_newton;
    ```

  Under `EncoderStrategy::Libjxl` the existing Section A `cfl_two_pass_min_effort
  = EffortGate::Libjxl` widening already fires Pass-2 at e>=5 (via
  `apply_section_a_effort_gates`), and `cfl_newton: effort >= 7` evaluates
  false at e=5/6 — so Pass-2 LS at e=5/6 was ALREADY happening on Libjxl
  before W44-197. The new gate is structurally redundant on `Libjxl` but
  provides an orthogonal axis for `Custom` strategy callers who want
  Pass-2 LS at e=5/6 WITHOUT the full Newton-at-e>=7 widening (Section A's
  EffortGate widens BOTH the e>=5 dispatch AND the Pass-2 inclusion).

- **Candidate C (perf, byte-identical default)**: closes W44-189 D13
  finding. Replaces per-coefficient `q / qw_x[i]` division in
  `refine_cfl_map` (`vardct/chroma_from_luma.rs:~597`) with multiplication
  `q * inv_qw_x[i]` where `inv_qw_x` is the existing precomputed reciprocal
  table from `quant::dequant_weights(strategy, channel)`. Mirrors libjxl
  `enc_chroma_from_luma.cc:337-343` which uses
  `Mul(qv, Load(df, qm_x + i))` with `qm_x = dequant.InvMatrix(...)`.

  Eliminates two f32 divisions per coefficient on the Pass-2 hot loop.
  At i8 CfL output granularity the multiplication form rounds to the same
  i8 multiplier as the division form on realistic inputs (a/b vs a*(1/b)
  differ at the last 1-2 bits of `qqm_x`; the dot products integrate over
  many coefficients and the final bias_and_quantize clamps to i8).

