Acceptance gates
----------------

(a) Build PASS
(b) `cargo test --lib --features '__expert __internals butteraugli-loop ssim2-loop parallel'`:
    1450/1450 PASS (count unchanged — W44-197 adds 1 unit test in
    gate_registry::tests::default_matches_zenjxl_byte_for_byte for the new
    field but it's part of the same `assert!()` body).
(c) Hash-locks 36/36 Zenjxl BYTE-IDENTICAL (Candidate C is pure perf at i8
    output granularity; Candidate B is gated to `Libjxl`-only).
(d) Libjxl byte-lock 4/4 BYTE-IDENTICAL (Cand B is structurally redundant
    on `Libjxl` per Section A widening; no cell shifts).
(e) `cargo test --test divergence_table_drift --features '__internals'`:
    7/7 PASS. `EXPECTED_DIVERGENCE_GATE_COUNT: 24 → 25`. New row added to
    `docs/LIBJXL_DIVERGENCES.md` Section C for `cfl_pass2_ls_at_low_effort`
    + perf row for D13 division→multiplication; D12 KNOWN-GAP row updated
    to RESOLVED via opt-in (W44-197).
(f) `cargo test --test strategy_libjxl_hash_locks` + multi-decoder
    roundtrip via jxl-rs + jxl-oxide on `libjxl_noise_rgb_48x48_d1`:
    5/5 + 1 ignored PASS. The Libjxl strategy output decodes cleanly on
    both decoders. (djxl validation deferred — test gated on binary
    availability; previous W44-195/196 djxl validation confirmed cleanly.)
(g) Candidate C perf measured: see TSV above. Wall-time delta on the
    sampled cells is within measurement noise at 0.25 MP — confirmed
    byte-identity at i8 output granularity is the load-bearing acceptance
    criterion. The per-coefficient division→multiplication replacement is
    a textbook perf win on modern f32 pipes (LLVM may auto-vectorize the
    multiplication form better, since the constant qw[i] is now loaded
    from a precomputed table and can sit in a register lane).
(h) Candidate B EV measured: bytes UNCHANGED on Libjxl byte-lock (Section A
    widening already fires the same dispatch path). Custom-strategy callers
    can now opt into the orthogonal Pass-2-LS-at-e=5/6 capability without
    flipping the Section A EffortGate.

What this RULES OUT (binding for future agents)
-----------------------------------------------

1. **DO NOT default-flip `cfl_pass2_ls_at_low_effort` on Zenjxl**. Same
   W44-29..W44-172 calibration concern as the W44-184 Pass-2 Newton flip
   (W44-183 measured 25/27 regressions). The default path stays at NO
   Pass-2 at e=5/6.

2. **DO NOT cite "FMA precision" for any byte difference here** (per user
   directive 2026-05-19 "it is never fma precision"). The Cand C change
   replaces division with multiplication using pre-computed reciprocals;
   the resulting f32 differs at the last 1-2 bits but rounds to the same
   i8 CfL output on realistic data.

3. **DO NOT remove the Pass-2 OOB-safety clamp** (`take = num_coeffs.min(buf_remaining)`).
   It's defensive against synthetic ac_strategy injections (e.g., GPU
   strat-search). W44-189 D14.

4. **DO NOT widen the Candidate B gate to non-Libjxl strategies without
   first re-running the W44-102 measurement with LS-only Pass-2 at e=5/6**.
   W44-102 ruled out FULL Newton widening; LS-only widening at e=5/6 was
   NEVER measured at the default path. The risk profile is unknown.

5. **DO NOT extend the W44-197 gate to the animation Pass-2 path
   (`bitstream.rs:1947`)**. Animation Zenjxl bitstream stability is
   the priority; W44-195 conservative pattern applies. Callers needing
   Pass-2 LS at e=5/6 in animation should opt in explicitly via Custom
   strategy + override (or future per-frame discriminator).

Follow-on candidates (NOT this chunk)
-------------------------------------

1. **Audit whether downstream W44-29..W44-172 cost-model calibration can
   be re-tuned for libjxl Pass-2 LS at e=5/6 at the default path.** Would
   close the W44-189 D12 row entirely (no opt-in needed). Multi-week
   effort tied to the same W44-184 cost-model retune candidate.

2. **Extend the W44-197 gate to animation paths** if a future per-frame
   discriminator surfaces a need. ~1 day chunk + animation hash-lock
   regen.

3. **W44-189 D9 AC metadata tree topology** (Section C, LOW-EV). At
   e>=8 (where libjxl doesn't pre-set TreeKind → falls back to `kLearn`
   for AC metadata), we could learn the tree adaptively. Probably not
   worth a chunk per W44-189 audit; the bytes are small (~50 B per DC
   group max).

